      "body": "\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Due to the large number of review comments, Critical severity comments were prioritized as inline comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🟠 Major comments (21)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>schemas/navigator-receipt-v1.schema.json-1-1 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-1`: _🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\n\n**Make each `primary` variant a closed, complete schema.**\n\nThis schema accepts incomplete receipts such as an `ordinary` receipt with `primary: {\"kind\":\"package_role\"}`. `validateNavigatorReceiptV1` requires `role`, `phase`, `evidenceIds`, `conditions`, and `hazards` for that variant.\n\nExpose the same closed discriminated union in this public schema. Otherwise schema consumers can accept receipts that the runtime rejects.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@schemas/navigator-receipt-v1.schema.json` at line 1, Update the\nstatus-dependent `primary` schemas in `NavigatorReceiptV1` so each discriminated\nvariant is closed and requires its complete variant-specific fields, matching\n`validateNavigatorReceiptV1`: ordinary variants must define all required fields\nfor `package_role`, `caller_action`, and `stop`, while insufficient, refused,\nand escalated variants must likewise require their complete payloads. Preserve\nthe existing status-to-kind constraints and prevent unspecified properties\nwithin each `primary` variant.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:a472aa4002e59e27535afa5d -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>schemas/assisted-call-v1.schema.json-14-14 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`14-14`: _🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Constrain `phase` by `role`.**\n\nThe schema accepts invalid configurations such as `{\"role\":\"judge\",\"phase\":\"apply\"}` and `{\"role\":\"coder\",\"phase\":null}`. This makes schema-valid caller input inconsistent with the package role contract.\n\nAdd conditional schema rules. Require `plan` or `apply` for `coder` and `fixer`. Require `null` for all other roles.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@schemas/assisted-call-v1.schema.json` at line 14, Update the execution\nschema’s role/phase validation so coder and fixer roles require phase to be plan\nor apply, while judge, reviewer, collector, and doctor require phase to be null.\nPreserve the existing role and phase value constraints and enforce the\nrelationship with conditional schema rules.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:52bb2ab69849d5b3cbf31031 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/navigator-contracts.ts-32-32 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`32-32`: _🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Reject duplicate evidence IDs in a snapshot.**\n\n`validateCurrentPositionSnapshotV1` permits multiple evidence records with the same `id`. `validateNavigatorReceiptV1` then indexes reads by that ID and validates citations against that non-unique namespace. A receipt can therefore appear to cite one evidence record while referring ambiguously to multiple frozen records.\n\nAdd a uniqueness check for `evidence.map((item) => item.id)` after parsing the evidence collection.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n const evidence = r.evidence.map(/* ... */);\n+if (new Set(evidence.map((item) => item.id)).size !== evidence.length)\n+  fail(\"unique evidence ids\");\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/navigator-contracts.ts` at line 32, Update\nvalidateCurrentPositionSnapshotV1 after parsing the evidence collection to\nreject duplicate evidence IDs by checking the uniqueness of evidence.map(item =>\nitem.id), using the existing fail path and preserving validation of unique\nevidence records.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:824bf3aa007a4b75fb95b87d -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/build-assisted.mjs-17-29 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`17-29`: _🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Emit all local runtime dependencies during the clean build.**\n\n`tsconfig.recorder.json` does not include `canonical-json.ts`, `sha256.ts`, or `compliance-transport.ts`. `build-assisted.mjs` uses `bundle: false` and lists none of these modules as entries. A clean package build therefore produces missing imports in `dist`. Add the dependencies as entries or enable bundling.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@scripts/build-assisted.mjs` around lines 17 - 29, Update the build\nconfiguration in build-assisted.mjs so local runtime dependencies such as\ncanonical-json.ts, sha256.ts, and compliance-transport.ts are emitted during a\nclean build. Either add these modules to the entries passed to build, or enable\nbundling while preserving the existing external-package behavior and\nimport-rewrite flow.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:c9abc98185fce7334a27f798 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/package-contracts/navigator-output.ts-2-3 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`2-3`: _🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Validate the complete recorded receipt contract.**\n\n`validateRecordedNavigatorReceiptV1` accepts arbitrary values for `subject`, `latestAttempt`, `explanation`, and each `evidenceRead` entry. `primary` only needs to be a non-null object, so an array passes. The validator also accepts negative cursors and does not validate UUIDv7 or digest formats.\n\nBecause Recorder extraction calls this validator for `ak_navigator_output`, malformed details can be persisted as an `AcceptedReceipt`. Reuse the canonical Navigator validator or add complete nested validators at this boundary.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/package-contracts/navigator-output.ts` around lines 2 - 3, Update\nvalidateRecordedNavigatorReceiptV1 to enforce the complete receipt contract by\nreusing the canonical Navigator validator, or by validating subject,\nlatestAttempt, explanation, every evidenceRead entry, and primary as the\nrequired non-array object shape. Also validate UUIDv7 runId/invocationId, the\nsnapshotDigest format, and require positionCursor to be a non-negative safe\ninteger before returning the receipt.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:e4e9bfd5adb316f04e573477 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/navigator-evidence.ts-3-3 (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`3-3`: _🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\n\n**Make UTF-8 page decoding safe at byte boundaries.**\n\n`offset` and `limit` are byte offsets. A valid UTF-8 code point can cross either boundary. `TextDecoder` with `fatal: true` then throws for valid evidence. The read set is updated before decoding, so a failed read can also record bytes as read.\n\nAlign pages to UTF-8 boundaries, retain decoder state, or expose byte-safe content. Update read state only after successful decoding.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/navigator-evidence.ts` at line 3, Update NavigatorEvidenceStore.read so\npaging never fatally decodes a valid UTF-8 sequence split across byte\nboundaries: align page boundaries, preserve decoder state, or return byte-safe\ncontent while maintaining the existing byte-based offsets and lengths. Ensure\ndecoding succeeds for valid evidence and move item.read updates until after\ncontent decoding completes successfully.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:662678183cd9b1ebbdcfaed0 -->\n\n---\n\n`3-3`: _🚀 Performance & Scalability_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\n\n**Bound total read-tracking memory.**\n\nThe per-page limit does not bound total tracking memory. `Set<number>` stores one JavaScript entry for every byte read. Reading a large admitted item can therefore consume substantially more memory than the evidence itself.\n\nTrack merged byte intervals or enforce a total evidence and read budget.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/navigator-evidence.ts` at line 3, Bound read-tracking memory in\nNavigatorEvidenceStore by replacing the per-byte Set<number> tracking with\nmerged byte intervals, or by enforcing an explicit total evidence/read budget.\nUpdate the read method to merge newly read ranges and update readRecord so\nfullyRead remains accurate without storing one entry per byte.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:a156ef54e3426b30dcdfaeec -->\n\n---\n\n`3-3`: _🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Clone admitted evidence bytes before storing them.**\n\n`sha256Hex(bytes)` validates the caller-owned `Uint8Array` only once. The store then keeps the same mutable buffer. A later mutation can make reads differ from `item.sha256`, so the evidence is no longer frozen.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-for(const item of evidence){const bytes=handles.get(item.handle);if(!bytes)throw new Error(`missing evidence handle: ${item.id}`);if(sha256Hex(bytes)!==item.sha256)throw new Error(`evidence digest mismatch: ${item.id}`);this.#byId.set(item.id,{bytes,read:new Set()})}\n+for(const item of evidence){const source=handles.get(item.handle);if(!source)throw new Error(`missing evidence handle: ${item.id}`);if(sha256Hex(source)!==item.sha256)throw new Error(`evidence digest mismatch: ${item.id}`);const bytes=new Uint8Array(source);this.#byId.set(item.id,{bytes,read:new Set()})}\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/navigator-evidence.ts` at line 3, Update the NavigatorEvidenceStore\nconstructor to clone each admitted Uint8Array before storing it in `#byId`, while\ncontinuing to validate the original bytes against item.sha256 first. Store and\nread from the clone so later caller mutations cannot alter admitted evidence.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:411c4e8b6f1695862c1d1c07 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/navigator-role.ts-5-5 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`5-5`: _🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Make Navigator activation transactional and fail closed.**\n\nA successful activation leaves `active` populated. If a later `activate()` call fails while loading the new snapshot or evidence, the previous snapshot remains available to the registered tools and `before_agent_start` handler. `registered` is also set before registration and verification complete.\n\nClear `active` before loading, build the next state locally, preflight tool names before registration, and commit `active` and `registered` only after all setup succeeds.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/navigator-role.ts` at line 5, Update createNavigatorRoleRuntime.activate\nto clear active before loading and construct the replacement state locally, so\nfailures cannot expose the previous snapshot. Preflight required tool names\nbefore registering tools, and move registered=true plus the active-state\nassignment until after registration and active-tool verification complete;\ncommit both only when the entire activation succeeds.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:05afb37d3c01c5b8fedb07d3 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/role-runtime.ts-251-256 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`251-256`: _🔒 Security & Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Constrain Navigator evidence handles before loading files.**\n\n`validateCurrentPositionSnapshotV1` accepts any non-empty `handle`, and the configured loader passes it directly to `readFile`. Absolute or traversal handles can therefore read arbitrary local files. Restrict handles to approved evidence or workspace roots and test both cases.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/role-runtime.ts` around lines 251 - 256, Constrain the Navigator evidence\nhandle before the loader reaches readFile: update the validation/loading flow\nused by createNavigatorRoleRuntime and validateCurrentPositionSnapshotV1 to\naccept only approved evidence handles or paths under the workspace roots,\nrejecting absolute and traversal paths. Preserve valid approved handles, and add\ntests covering both accepted rooted handles and rejected absolute/traversal\nhandles.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:1bb67ccdd36af963968769d7 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/assisted-ledger.ts-6-6 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`6-6`: _🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\n\n**Do not delete live temporary generations during append.**\n\nWhen two appenders overlap, a later append can unlink an earlier appender’s open `.tmp-*` path. The earlier append then receives `ENOENT` from `renameNoReplace` instead of `AssistedLedgerConflictError`. Clean only files proven stale, or move cleanup to recovery.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/assisted-ledger.ts` at line 6, The cleanup loop in\nappendAssistedGenerationV1 must not unlink live .tmp-* files created by\noverlapping appenders. Remove this unconditional startup deletion or replace it\nwith cleanup that can prove a temporary file is stale; preserve conflict\nhandling so an overlapping append results in AssistedLedgerConflictError rather\nthan ENOENT from renameNoReplace.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:4a866b542581ab2ce064efd4 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/assisted-acquisition.ts-6-6 (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`6-6`: _🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Reject collisions with generated evidence IDs.**\n\nA caller can declare `parent-issue-body` or `child-<number>-issue-body`. `admit` then creates the same ID, because validation only checks duplicates within caller-declared evidence. This produces duplicate snapshot entries and makes evidence lookup ambiguous.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n const handles = new Map<string, Uint8Array>();\n const evidence = [];\n+const evidenceIds = new Set<string>();\n+\n function admit(id, kind, bytes, reference, handle) {\n+  if (evidenceIds.has(id)) throw new Error(\"duplicate evidence id\");\n+  evidenceIds.add(id);\n   handles.set(handle, bytes);\n   evidence.push({id, kind, sha256: sha256Hex(bytes), provenance: {kind: \"acquired\", reference}, handle});\n }\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/assisted-acquisition.ts` at line 6, Update acquireCurrentPositionV1 and\nits admit flow to reserve the generated parent-issue-body and\nchild-<number>-issue-body IDs before admitting caller-declared evidence. Reject\nany declared evidence whose id collides with these generated IDs, while\npreserving duplicate rejection among caller-declared evidence and ensuring the\nsnapshot contains unique evidence IDs.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:a0a5931a755734732bfba652 -->\n\n---\n\n`6-6`: _🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Bound declared evidence before loading it.** `readFile(d.path)` loads the complete caller-selected path before Navigator applies its page limit. Reject non-regular files and enforce `MAX_EVIDENCE_BYTES` during a bounded descriptor read. A preliminary `lstat` followed by unbounded `readFile` does not prevent races or memory exhaustion.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/assisted-acquisition.ts` at line 6, Update acquireCurrentPositionV1’s\nconfig.acquisition.evidence loading path to validate each declared path as a\nregular file and read it through a bounded descriptor-based operation capped at\nMAX_EVIDENCE_BYTES. Replace the unbounded readFile(d.path) usage; enforce the\nlimit while reading after opening the file so path races cannot bypass\nvalidation or cause excessive memory allocation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:07c7c2fae106ccb0ddaf3ce5 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/assisted-contracts.ts-7-7 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`7-7`: _🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Reject non-string and non-canonical path values.**\n\n`String(w.root)` and `String(declaration.path)` allow arrays and non-canonical strings through. Acquisition then passes invalid values to `observeWorkspace` or `readFile`, causing runtime `TypeError` failures. Require `typeof value === \"string\"`, `isAbsolute(value)`, and `resolve(value) === value` for workspace roots and evidence paths.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/assisted-contracts.ts` at line 7, Update validateAssistedCallConfigV1 to\nvalidate workspace roots and evidence paths directly as strings: require typeof\nvalue === \"string\", isAbsolute(value), and resolve(value) === value. Remove the\nString(...) coercions for w.root and declaration.path so arrays and other\nnon-string values are rejected before downstream use.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:721e227e3ed5b65b99c9381c -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/assisted-contracts.ts-10-10 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`10-10`: _🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Complete `assistedCallConfigV1Schema`.**\n\n`additionalProperties: false` is set without `properties` or `patternProperties`. Therefore every top-level config key is rejected. Define the top-level and nested schemas, consistent with `schemas/assisted-call-v1.schema.json`, or remove this export.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/assisted-contracts.ts` at line 10, Complete assistedCallConfigV1Schema by\ndefining properties for all required top-level fields—version, runId, callId,\nsubject, acquisition, and execution—and their nested structures to match\nschemas/assisted-call-v1.schema.json, while retaining additionalProperties:\nfalse. If the schema cannot be completed consistently, remove this export\ninstead.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:974511c9aa5379818848430c -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/assisted-acquisition.ts-1-4 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-4`: _🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Bound all Git and GitHub CLI calls.**\n\nSet a finite `timeout` on both `git` calls and the shared `gh api` call. Without it, a stalled process can block acquisition, resume, or recovery indefinitely. Preserve timeout rejections as failures.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/assisted-acquisition.ts` around lines 1 - 4, Set a finite timeout option\non both exec calls in createGitCliTransportV1.observeWorkspace and on the shared\nexec call inside createGhJsonTransportV1.api. Use the same bounded timeout\nconfiguration for all Git and GitHub CLI invocations, while allowing timeout\nerrors to propagate unchanged as failures.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:b8d110386152c5466a6dfa47 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/assisted-runner.ts-4-4 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`4-4`: _🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Add a retry cap and backoff to the ledger-append retry loop.**\n\n`appendAssistedGenerationV1` retries in a `for(;;)` loop on every `AssistedLedgerConflictError`, with no maximum attempt count and no delay between attempts. Under sustained write contention (several concurrent callers, or a persistent unhandled conflict shape not covered by the classification checks), this loop can spin indefinitely, generating continuous filesystem reads/writes without yielding.\n\nAdd a bounded retry count with jittered backoff, and fail with a clear error once the bound is exceeded.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the\nrest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn `@src/assisted-runner.ts` at line 4, Update appendAssistedGenerationV1 to\nreplace its unbounded for(;;) retry loop with a finite attempt limit, applying\njittered backoff before retrying AssistedLedgerConflictError failures. Preserve\nexisting conflict classification and propagation behavior, and throw a clear\nerror when the retry bound is exhausted.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- cr-comment:v1:53e50276eaf9590e84f6cb57 -->\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/assisted-runner.ts-19-19 (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`19-19`: _🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Replace error-message string matching with a typed exception.**\n\n`recoverAssistedInvocationV1` detects an already-recovered outcome by checking `error.message===\"compatible assisted lifecycle transition already owned for recovered\"`. This message is generated dynamically in `appendAssistedGenerationV1` (Line 4) via a template literal built from `event.type`. Coupling recovery control flow to this exact string is fragile: if the message text changes, the reconciliation silently stops working and a real recovery failure could surface as an unhandled crash, or, conversely, an unrelated error with the same text could be misclassified as a benign already-recovered outcome.\n\nUse a typed signal instead, matching the existing `CanonicalLifecycleResult` pattern already used elsewhere in this file for the same purpose.\n\n\n\n\n\nBased on coding guidelines: \"Machines must consume contracts rather than presentation: do not mechanically depend on free-text regexes, wording, headers, or image pixels; expose machine-consumed information through keys, typed fields, or schemas.\"\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed typed-signal fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-class CanonicalLifecycleResult extends Error{constructor(readonly result:AssistedCallResultV1){super(\"canonical assisted result won publication\")}}\n+class CanonicalLifecycleResult extends Error{constructor(readonly result:AssistedCallResultV1){super(\"canonical assisted result won publication\")}}\n+class AlreadyRecoveredSignal extends Error{constructor(readonly invocationId:string){super(\"compatible recovered transition already owned\")}}\n```\n```diff\n-if([\"call_started\",\"navigator_started\",\"action_reserved\",\"role_started\",\"recovered\"].includes(event.type))throw new Error(`compatible assisted lifecycle transition already owned for ${event.type}`);\n+if(event.type===\"recovered\")throw new AlreadyRecoveredSignal(event.invocationId!);\n+if([\"call_started\",\"navigator_started\",\"action_reserved\",\"role_started\"].includes(event.type))throw new Error(`compatible assisted lifecycle transition already owned for ${event.type}`);\n```\n```diff\n-export async function recoverAssistedInvocationV1(repositoryRoot:string,runId:string,invocationId:string,confirmedStopped:boolean,deps:AssistedRunnerDependenciesV1){try{return await recoverAssistedInvocationInternalV1(repositoryRoot,runId,invocationId,confirmedStopped,deps)}catch(error){if(error instanceof CanonicalLifecycleResult||error instanceof Error&&error.message===\"compatible assisted lifecycle transition already owned for recovered\")return readAssistedRunV1(repositoryRoot,runId);throw error}}\n+export async function recoverAssistedInvocationV1(repositoryRoot:string,runId:string,invocationId:string,confirmedStopped:boolean,deps:AssistedRunnerDependenciesV1){try{return await recoverAssistedInvocationInternalV1(repositoryRoot,runId,invocationId,confirmedStopped,deps)}catch(error){if(error instanceof CanonicalLifecycleResult||error instanceof AlreadyRecoveredSignal)return readAssistedRunV1(repositoryRoot,runId);throw error}}\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summa